      "content": "Common screen reader failures include missing or vague labels for non-text content like icons, preventing users from understanding their function. Another frequent issue is incorrect reading order, where the screen reader jumps through the DOM in an illogical sequence, confusing the user. Finally, dynamic content updates, such as error messages, often fail to announce themselves unless proper ARIA live regions are implemented.",
